# Configuration

Before you start integrating with the Codexeron platform, you should properly configure your development environment.

This guide explains the basic configuration required for secure and reliable communication with Codexeron services.

---

# Overview

This guide covers:

- API configuration
- API Keys
- Base URL
- Environment variables
- HTTPS requirements
- Security recommendations

---

# Base URL

All API requests must be sent to the official Codexeron API endpoint.

Example:

```
https://api.codexeron.com
```

> **Note**
>
> The API base URL may change in future major releases. Always refer to the latest API documentation.

---

# Authentication

All protected endpoints require authentication.

Authentication is performed using an API Key.

Never expose your API Key publicly.

---

# Environment Variables

Store sensitive configuration values using environment variables.

Example variables:

```
CODEXERON_API_KEY=your_api_key

CODEXERON_API_URL=https://api.codexeron.com

CODEXERON_TIMEOUT=30
```

---

# HTTPS

All communication with Codexeron services must use HTTPS.

HTTP connections are not supported.

---

# Request Timeout

Recommended timeout values:

| Type | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Connection Timeout | 10 seconds |
| Request Timeout | 30 seconds |

Applications with long-running requests should implement retry logic.

---

# API Key Security

Always follow these recommendations:

- Never hardcode API keys.
- Never publish API keys.
- Rotate API keys regularly.
- Store credentials securely.
- Use separate API keys for development and production environments.

---

# Error Handling

Applications should gracefully handle:

- Authentication failures
- Network failures
- Rate limit responses
- Timeout errors
- Temporary server errors

Always validate API responses before processing data.

---

# Logging

Avoid logging:

- API Keys
- Authentication tokens
- User credentials
- Sensitive personal information

Logs should contain only the information required for debugging.

---

# Best Practices

For a reliable integration:

- Keep dependencies updated.
- Always use HTTPS.
- Validate all responses.
- Handle exceptions correctly.
- Monitor API usage.
- Respect rate limits.

---

# Verify Your Configuration

Before continuing, confirm:

- API URL configured
- API Key stored securely
- HTTPS enabled
- Timeout configured
- Environment variables created

If everything above is complete, your application is ready to communicate with Codexeron services.

